8.4 Daytime Analysis of $SNDK
SNDK, supported by the 1265 USD bottom support, completed a deep-V reversal. The medium-term rebound trend is clear. After a short-term push to a higher level, it has entered a phase of mild consolidation and washing. Overall, the core trading idea is to go long on pullbacks at lower levels. Be cautious about chasing highs at elevated prices, and prepare risk-control plans around key support levels to deal with overnight uncertainty in the US stock market. 

Medium-term pattern: On the weekly chart, a standard deep-V reversal structure has formed. After the prior low was tested at 1265.00 USD, it stabilized and began basing. Going forward, the subsequent lows keep rising and the rebound steps upward, so the medium-term rebound trend framework remains solid;

Short-term rhythm: In this rebound, the high reached 1337.00 USD, then it fell slightly. This is normal profit-taking digestion after the spike, not a signal of a trend reversal;

Volume and price characteristics: During the rebound phase, bullish candles have strong continuity. Pullback candles are relatively small in body volume, and the market’s upward-dominated rhythm has not been broken. 

